Z||000000||jhar1987||04-03-2001||07:27 PM||||my 2.8 won't idle and it is showing no codes? it starts fine and as long as you keep your foot in it it stays running. let off the accel. and she dies?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||04-03-2001||07:41 PM||||Check your distributor. I was replacing the pick-up coil when I noticed the reluctor was craked. When I took it off it broke completly in half. I put it back on, because I can't get a new one without buying a new distributor, and now the car is dieing just like yours is. It could either be the reluctor or the Pick-up coil. Pray it is the pickup coil because you can't get a new reluctor without buying a whole new distributor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ka4nkf||04-05-2001||11:52 PM||||I don't think it would be the dist. pick up coil, if it is bad it wont run at all. I would check the throtle position sensor. I know it is supposed to send a code, but I have found sometimes if the sensor is not completly shot it won't throw a code.<BR>Good luck<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric_PA||04-05-2001||11:57 PM||||I had a problem like this. I found that it was a bad EGR. No codes where set and ran fine once I was on the gas, but would stall at stop lights. This was on an 86 2.8 Automatic.<P>Eric||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||04-06-2001||12:11 AM||||Bad EGR, Clogged IAC port, Clogged vaccum port, Bad TPS, Dirty injectors, just to name a few things to check.||||reg||1
